      "confidence": 0.9,
      "curator_note": "Cross-linked MOD rule variable: IMS_4_14, DFS '[C]1([C]2[C]3)([C]4[C]5){=}[O+.]>>[C.]2[C]3.[C]4[C]5[C]1{#}[O+]'. Verified against this scheme rather than asserted: the DFS cleaves the C1-C2 bond (carbonyl carbon to the alpha carbon of one ethyl) and raises the C1-O bond from double to triple, i.e. the cleaved sigma bond IS incident to the atom that gains bond order, matching the two bond changes encoded here; the departing ethyl is written [C.]2[C]3 (radical) and the charge stays on oxygen, as in the book. RDKit check: the rule's left-hand pattern [#6](-[#6]-[#6])(-[#6]-[#6])=[O+] matches the instantiated precursor [CH3:1][CH2:2][C:3](=[O+:4])[CH2:5][CH3:6] (True). The rule survives the conservation guardrail (kept at import)."
